                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]A Indie Developer Simulator / Platformer Editor[/h1]\nhttps://youtu.be/nnm2ARAcSJ0\n+ The gameplay is pretty fun. You mainly design, test, and play a variety of platforming levels or \"games\", and then publish your work on the market to make money to purchase additional assets to make your next game even better! \n+ Although very basic, it is a interesting look at some of the things that goes into being a indie game developer and fun to read through the mock steam reviews.\n+ Gets a bit deep, and questions why you want to be a indie game developer when there's so many other people doing the same thing. What makes you so special? \n\n- Earning money for additional assets for your games is a bit of a grind, especially considering you have to pay for every tile you place in your game which limits your creativity a bit.\n- It's a bit unclear as to what your game needs to get a high rating (which is needed to get high sales / money)",
